@startuml
' Rendered by scripts/build-diagrams.sh. Edit this file, never the SVG beside it.
'
' One neutral grey on a transparent background, so a single SVG stays legible on
' the light theme and the dark one. Nothing here picks a palette, which is what
' lets the site own its own colors.
<style>
document {
  BackgroundColor transparent
}
sequenceDiagram {
  BackgroundColor transparent
  LineColor #888888
  FontColor #888888
  FontName Helvetica
  FontSize 13

  participant {
    BackgroundColor transparent
    LineColor #888888
    FontColor #888888
  }
  lifeLine {
    BackgroundColor transparent
    LineColor #888888
  }
  note {
    BackgroundColor transparent
    LineColor #888888
    FontColor #888888
  }
  arrow {
    LineColor #888888
    FontColor #888888
  }
  group {
    BackgroundColor transparent
    LineColor #888888
    FontColor #888888
  }
  divider {
    BackgroundColor transparent
    LineColor #888888
    FontColor #888888
  }
}
</style>
skinparam shadowing false
hide footbox

' A period in a participant name is a namespace separator to PlantUML, which
' splits a label into two boxes. Turned off so a label is a label.
set separator none

participant "Client" as Client
participant "routes.php\ngenerated" as Route
participant "the scope middleware" as Scope
participant "Controllers\\UserController\nyours" as Child
participant "Generated\\Controllers\\UserController\ngenerated" as Parent
participant "UserDtoFactory\ngenerated" as Factory

note over Scope, Factory
  Phase 2, not shipped: the scope middleware,
  the DTO and its factory. Today routeAction
  throws and Laravel renders 501 until a custom
  child answers.
end note

Client -> Route : GET /users/42
Route -> Route : implicit binding\nresolves User 42
Route -> Scope : does the model\nhave the scope?
Scope --> Route : yes
Route -> Child : routeAction(User)

note over Route, Child
  The route points at your class when its file
  exists, and at the generated parent when it
  does not. Decided at build time, so
  route:cache keeps working.
end note

Child -> Parent : parent::routeAction(User)
Parent -> Parent : respondWithSingle(User)
Parent -> Factory : from(User)
Factory --> Parent : UserDto
Parent --> Child : UserDto
Child --> Client : 200, the response schema's shape


@enduml
